reaper_test.go     |  32 ++++++\n internal/state/usage.go           |  16 ++-\n internal/state/usage_test.go      |  20 ++++\n 13 files changed, 565 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n\ndiff --git a/docs/proposal.md b/docs/proposal.md\nindex d2bfe76..496449b 100644\n--- a/docs/proposal.md\n+++ b/docs/proposal.md\n@@ -495,7 +495,7 @@ Agents with push access read text that strangers can write, so the controls sit\n - **Budgets.** Every job has a dollar cap (`max_budget_usd`) and a hard timeout; every role and the whole repo have a daily dollar cap. The caps are enforced at the pool's claim gate (`internal/budget`): a candidate is refused when `spent >= cap`, where spent is the cost recorded in `step_usage` since 00:00 UTC today. The caps reset at 00:00 UTC and survive a restart, because spend is read from the controller database. A role's own `budget_usd_per_day` caps that role (by stage and name) alone; a role without one is limited only by the repo cap. Steps that reported no cost count as $0, and the refusal reason shows how many there were. There is no exemption for reviewers, the caps apply to OAuth credentials too, and deterministic scanners (no model, no cost) are exempt. Running jobs are never killed for a cap. If today's spend cannot be read, the gate refuses (fails closed). Each cap is logged once a day as `budget.capped`. The `budget` loop posts one comment on the status issue per capped scope (the repo, or a role) per UTC day, and records a `budget_capped` event; that event also keeps a restart from posting the notice again (a crash between comment and event can repeat one notice). The comment holds only numbers, the day and config names, no agent text and no `@`; it says the dollar figure is an estimate on a subscription and how to raise the cap (edit `budget_usd_per_day` in `.ard/config.yaml` through a reviewed PR). Under `--dry-run` the comment goes to the ledger. `--loops budget` selects the notice loop; the gate is part of the pool and is always on.\n - **Concurrency.** `max_pods` (default 3) caps every job together, and at most one triage job runs per issue at a time, because triage roles share `plan.md`; no triage job is claimed for an issue while a worker job runs on it.\n - **Kill switch.** Four sources stop new claims, scanner runs (filing and autoclose), stale closes and merges: a local pause file `~/.ard/pause/<owner>/<repo>` outside the repository (the path is lowercased; `ard serve` creates the directory, so `touch` pauses and `rm` resumes), `paused: true` in the `config.yaml` in the host's working tree, `ard:pause` on the pinned status issue, and `paused: true` in the config on `origin/main`. They are checked cheapest first, before every claiming tick. The delay is at most one loop interval plus 10% jitter; a tick already running may finish its claims. `SIGUSR1` (Unix only) makes every loop run one tick now, logged as `controller.wake`; the tick still passes the kill switch and the job pool, and wakes that arrive while a tick runs coalesce into one extra tick. The gate answers one controller-wide question and has no per-kind checks, so every loop that writes (scanner filing and autoclose, stale closes, merges, claims), except the Reaper, the cost-table writer and in-flight close-outs, must report `Claims() == true` and is skipped while paused. Running jobs, in-flight close-outs, the Reaper and the `costs` loop continue: the table is bookkeeping about work already done, not new work. The check fails closed: an unreadable status issue, a failed fetch of `origin/main`, or a config that fails to load counts as paused. The pause file pauses when anything exists at the path (a file, a directory or a symlink; content is ignored), and a path that cannot be examined, for example because `pause/<owner>` is a regular file, also counts as paused. The local working-tree `config.yaml` is read only for its `paused` key; a missing, unreadable or invalid file does not pause by itself, but a readable one that says `paused: true` does. The pause file and the local `paused` are the kill switches that nothing pushed to GitHub can lift. Config and role directories otherwise come from `origin/main` at the same SHA the tick's jobs use (see Configuration). `ard serve` remembers the status issue number in `_controller.db` (`meta` key `status_issue`). At startup it reads that issue directly and adopts it if it is still open, titled `ard status`, carries the `<!-- ard:status -->` marker and has the App as author; otherwise it searches by those same tests, and creates and pins the issue if none matches. Search is eventually consistent, so the remembered number is what stops a quick restart from creating a second issue; if two still match, the lowest number wins. A cached issue that cannot be read for a reason other than not-found falls back to search rather than aborting startup. A dry-run never stores its synthetic (negative) number; a real number found by search is stored only in the separate dry-run database. A second `ard serve` on the same repo exits with an error: the leader lock is an `flock` on `~/.ard/locks/<owner>/<repo>.lock` (local filesystem only), shared by live and dry-run.\n-- **Observability.** Every claim, close-out and failure is an event in local state. A daily digest on the pinned status issue shows queue depth by label, jobs run, failures and spend. Each issue's body also carries a per-job cost table (agent, tokens by type, cost, model, outcome and a link to the job's comment, PR) with a Total row, written by the `costs` loop. A reached daily cap is a `budget_capped` event. The repository may be public, so the spend it shows is public too; the table holds no agent text or host paths. Scanner failure streaks (#221, the early slice of the digest, #58): each scanner posts one comment on the status issue when a failure streak starts and one when it recovers. A streak starts at the first run that is a guard trip or guard error (reason: the guard rule name or `scan-error`), any other `scan_failed` run (a `timeout` counts as `scan_failed`) or a skip at `max_open`, and ends at the next `ok` run. The posted class is kept in the scanner's `meta` table (key `failure_streak`), so a restart does not repost, and it is written only after the post succeeds. Runs dropped at the global cap and `error` runs neither start nor end a streak. A comment carries the scanner name and the reason class only, never finding text, titles, fingerprints or log lines. The post goes through the effect layer, so a dry-run logs it (`scanner.streak_notice`) and stores no streak. While the status issue number is unknown nothing is posted and the streak is not recorded, so it posts once the issue exists.\n+- **Observability.** Every claim, close-out and failure is an event in local state. A daily digest on the pinned status issue shows queue depth by label, jobs run, failures and spend. Each issue's body also carries a per-job cost table (agent, tokens by type, cost, model, outcome and a link to the job's comment, PR) with a Total row, written by the `costs` loop. The digest is a `digest` loop that posts one new comment a day on the status issue, titled \"daily digest for <date> (UTC)\", covering the previous complete UTC day: open-issue counts per `ard:` label, jobs run, failures (with a per-role split) and spend. A `digest` event written after the post is the once-per-day marker, so a restart does not repost; it holds numbers, label and role names only. A reached daily cap is a `budget_capped` event. The repository may be public, so the spend it shows is public too; the table holds no agent text or host paths. Scanner failure streaks (#221, the early slice of the digest, #58): each scanner posts one comment on the status issue when a failure streak starts and one when it recovers. A streak starts at the first run that is a guard trip or guard error (reason: the guard rule name or `scan-error`), any other `scan_failed` run (a `timeout` counts as `scan_failed`) or a skip at `max_open`, and ends at the next `ok` run. The posted class is kept in the scanner's `meta` table (key `failure_streak`), so a restart does not repost, and it is written only after the post succeeds. Runs dropped at the global cap and `error` runs neither start nor end a streak. A comment carries the scanner name and the reason class only, never finding text, titles, fingerprints or log lines. The post goes through the effect layer, so a dry-run logs it (`scanner.streak_notice`) and stores no streak. While the status issue number is unknown nothing is posted and the streak is not recorded, so it posts once the issue exists.\n \n ## Gaps in the original sketch\n \ndiff --git a/internal/digest/digest.go b/internal/digest/digest.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..d632749\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/digest/digest.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@\n+// Package digest posts the daily status-issue digest: queue depth by label,\n+// jobs run, failures and spend for the previous UTC day.\n+package digest\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"log/slog\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"sync\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n+)\n+\n+// Name is the digest loop's name, as --loops spells it.\n+const Name = \"digest\"\n+\n+// Store is the part of *state.Store the loop uses.\n+type Store interface {\n+\tAppendEvent(ctx context.Context, e state.Event) error\n+\tEvents(ctx context.Context, f state.EventFilter) ([]state.Event, error)\n+\tCountEndedSince(ctx context.Context, since, until time.Time) (map[state.RoleKey]state.JobCounts, error)\n+\tSpendBetween(ctx context.Context, from, to time.Time) (map[state.RoleKey]state.Spend, state.Spend, error)\n+}\n+\n+// Reader lists issues for the queue depth.\n+type Reader interface {\n+\tListIssues(ctx context.Context, o github.ListIssuesOpts) ([]github.Issue, error)\n+}\n+\n+// Effects is the part of effects.Effects the loop uses.\n+type Effects interface {\n+\tCreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error)\n+\tDryRun() bool\n+}\n+\n+// Deps are the loop's collaborators. StatusIssue returns 0 until the status\n+// issue is known. Now nil means time.Now; Log nil means slog.Default.\n+type Deps struct {\n+\tStore       Store\n+\tReader      Reader\n+\tEffects     Effects\n+\tStatusIssue func() int\n+\tLog         *slog.Logger\n+\tNow         func() time.Time\n+}\n+\n+// Loop posts one digest comment per UTC day. The digest event written after\n+// the comment is the marker that keeps a restart from posting it again.\n+type Loop struct {\n+\td  Deps\n+\tmu sync.Mutex\n+}\n+\n+// NewLoop builds the digest loop.\n+func NewLoop(d Deps) *Loop {\n+\tif d.Now == nil {\n+\t\td.Now = time.Now\n+\t}\n+\tif d.Log == nil {\n+\t\td.Log = slog.Default()\n+\t}\n+\treturn &Loop{d: d}\n+}\n+\n+// Name implements controller.Loop.\n+func (*Loop) Name() string { return Name }\n+\n+// Interval implements controller.Loop.\n+func (*Loop) Interval(*config.Resolved) time.Duration { return 10 * time.Minute }\n+\n+// Claims is false: the digest is bookkeeping and runs while paused.\n+func (*Loop) Claims() bool { return false }\n+\n+var _ controller.Loop = (*Loop)(nil)\n+\n+// Tick posts today's digest when it is not yet posted.\n+func (l *Loop) Tick(ctx context.Context, _ controller.Env) error {\n+\tl.mu.Lock()\n+\tdefer l.mu.Unlock()\n+\tissue := l.d.StatusIssue()\n+\tif issue == 0 {\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tnow := l.d.Now().UTC()\n+\ttoday := time.Date(now.Year(), now.Month(), now.Day(), 0, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)\n+\tfrom := today.Add(-24 * time.Hour)\n+\tday := from.Format(\"2006-01-02\")\n+\n+\tevs, err := l.d.Store.Events(ctx, state.EventFilter{Kind: state.EventDigest, Since: today})\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"digest: read events: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, e := range evs {\n+\t\tvar d struct {\n+\t\t\tDay string `json:\"day\"`\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif json.Unmarshal(e.Data, &d) == nil && d.Day == day {\n+\t\t\treturn nil\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\n+\tissues, err := l.d.Reader.ListIssues(ctx, github.ListIssuesOpts{State: github.StateOpen})\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"digest: list issues: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tqueue := map[string]int{}\n+\tfor _, is := range issues {\n+\t\tif is.IsPR {\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tfor _, lb := range is.Labels {\n+\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(lb, labels.Prefix) {\n+\t\t\t\tqueue[lb]++\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tjobs, err := l.d.Store.CountEndedSince(ctx, from, today)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"digest: count jobs: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tperSpend, spend, err := l.d.Store.SpendBetween(ctx, from, today)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"digest: read spend: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tdata := Data{Day: day, Queue: queue, Jobs: jobs, Spend: perSpend, Total: spend}\n+\tif l.d.Effects.DryRun() {\n+\t\tl.d.Log.Info(\"digest.notice\", \"day\", day)\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := l.d.Effects.CreateComment(ctx, issue, Render(data)); err != nil {\n+\t\tl.d.Log.Error(\"digest.post_failed\", \"day\", day, \"error\", err)\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tnJobs, nFail := data.counts()\n+\tev, _ := json.Marshal(map[string]any{\n+\t\t\"day\": day, \"jobs\": nJobs, \"failures\": nFail, \"spend_usd\": spend.USD, \"unpriced\": spend.Unpriced,\n+\t})\n+\tif err := l.d.Store.AppendEvent(ctx, state.Event{At: l.d.Now(), Kind: state.EventDigest, Data: ev}); err != nil {\n+\t\tl.d.Log.Error(\"digest.unrecorded\", \"day\", day, \"error\", err)\n+\t}\n+\treturn nil\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/digest/digest_test.go b/internal/digest/digest_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f9faac1\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/digest/digest_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,201 @@\n+package digest\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n+)\n+\n+type fakeStore struct {\n+\tevents   []state.Event\n+\tfrom, to time.Time\n+\tjobs     map[state.RoleKey]state.JobCounts\n+\tspend    state.Spend\n+}\n+\n+func (f *fakeStore) AppendEvent(_ context.Context, e state.Event) error {\n+\tf.events = append(f.events, e)\n+\treturn nil\n+}\n+\n+func (f *fakeStore) Events(_ context.Context, fl state.EventFilter) ([]state.Event, error) {\n+\tvar out []state.Event\n+\tfor _, e := range f.events {\n+\t\tif e.Kind == fl.Kind && !e.At.Before(fl.Since) {\n+\t\t\tout = append(out, e)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn out, nil\n+}\n+\n+func (f *fakeStore) CountEndedSince(_ context.Context, from, to time.Time) (map[state.RoleKey]state.JobCounts, error) {\n+\tf.from, f.to = from, to\n+\treturn f.jobs, nil\n+}\n+\n+func (f *fakeStore) SpendBetween(context.Context, time.Time, time.Time) (map[state.RoleKey]state.Spend, state.Spend, error) {\n+\treturn nil, f.spend, nil\n+}\n+\n+type fakeReader struct {\n+\tissues []github.Issue\n+\terr    error\n+}\n+\n+func (r fakeReader) ListIssues(context.Context, github.ListIssuesOpts) ([]github.Issue, error) {\n+\treturn r.issues, r.err\n+}\n+\n+type fakeEffects struct {\n+\tbodies []string\n+\terr    error\n+\tdry    bool\n+}\n+\n+func (e *fakeEffects) CreateComment(_ context.Context, _ int, body string) (github.Comment, error) {\n+\tif e.err != nil {\n+\t\treturn github.Comment{}, e.err\n+\t}\n+\te.bodies = append(e.bodies, body)\n+\treturn github.Comment{}, nil\n+}\n+func (e *fakeEffects) DryRun() bool { return e.dry }\n+\n+func setup(now *time.Time) (*Loop, *fakeStore, *fakeEffects, *fakeReader) {\n+\tst := &fakeStore{}\n+\tfx := &fakeEffects{}\n+\trd := &fakeReader{}\n+\tl := NewLoop(Deps{Store: st, Reader: rd, Effects: fx, StatusIssue: func() int { return 1 }, Now: func() time.Time { return *now }})\n+\treturn l, st, fx, rd\n+}\n+\n+var noon = time.Date(2026, 3, 5, 12, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)\n+\n+func TestTickPostsOnce(t *testing.T) {\n+\tnow := noon\n+\tl, st, fx, _ := setup(&now)\n+\tfor i := 0; i < 2; i++ {\n+\t\tif err := l.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv()); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif len(fx.bodies) != 1 || len(st.events) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"posts = %d, events = %d; want 1, 1\", len(fx.bodies), len(st.events))\n+\t}\n+\tif !strings.Contains(fx.bodies[0], \"day=2026-03-04\") {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"body = %q\", fx.bodies[0])\n+\t}\n+\t// Restart: a new loop over the same store posts nothing; the next day posts.\n+\tl2 := NewLoop(l.d)\n+\t_ = l2.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv())\n+\tif len(fx.bodies) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"restart reposted\")\n+\t}\n+\tnow = noon.Add(24 * time.Hour)\n+\t_ = l2.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv())\n+\tif len(fx.bodies) != 2 {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"next day posts = %d, want 2\", len(fx.bodies))\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestTickNoStatusIssue(t *testing.T) {\n+\tnow := noon\n+\tl, st, fx, _ := setup(&now)\n+\tl.d.StatusIssue = func() int { return 0 }\n+\t_ = l.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv())\n+\tif len(fx.bodies)+len(st.events) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Error(\"posted without a status issue\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestTickPostFailsNoEvent(t *testing.T) {\n+\tnow := noon\n+\tl, st, fx, _ := setup(&now)\n+\tfx.err = errors.New(\"boom\")\n+\t_ = l.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv())\n+\tif len(st.events) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"event stored after a failed post\")\n+\t}\n+\tfx.err = nil\n+\t_ = l.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv())\n+\tif len(fx.bodies) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Error(\"no retry\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestTickDryRun(t *testing.T) {\n+\tnow := noon\n+\tl, st, fx, _ := setup(&now)\n+\tfx.dry = true\n+\t_ = l.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv())\n+\tif len(fx.bodies)+len(st.events) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Error(\"dry run posted or stored\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestTickReaderError(t *testing.T) {\n+\tnow := noon\n+\tl, _, fx, rd := setup(&now)\n+\trd.err = errors.New(\"api\")\n+\tif err := l.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv()); err == nil || len(fx.bodies) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"err = %v, posts = %d\", err, len(fx.bodies))\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestWindowPreviousDay(t *testing.T) {\n+\tnow := noon\n+\tl, st, _, _ := setup(&now)\n+\t_ = l.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv())\n+\tif !st.from.Equal(time.Date(2026, 3, 4, 0, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)) || !st.to.Equal(time.Date(2026, 3, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)) {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"window = [%v, %v)\", st.from, st.to)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestQueueDepthByLabel(t *testing.T) {\n+\tnow := noon\n+\tl, _, fx, rd := setup(&now)\n+\trd.issues = []github.Issue{\n+\t\t{Number: 2, Labels: []string{\"ard:pending\", \"bug\"}},\n+\t\t{Number: 3, Labels: []string{\"ard:pending\", \"ard:hold\"}},\n+\t\t{Number: 4, IsPR: true, Labels: []string{\"ard:hold\"}},\n+\t}\n+\t_ = l.Tick(context.Background(), controllerEnv())\n+\tb := fx.bodies[0]\n+\tif !strings.Contains(b, \"| `ard:pending` | 2 |\") || !strings.Contains(b, \"| `ard:hold` | 1 |\") || strings.Contains(b, \"bug\") {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"body = %s\", b)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestRenderZeroAndUnsafe(t *testing.T) {\n+\tzero := Render(Data{Day: \"2026-03-04\"})\n+\tfor _, want := range []string{\"<!-- ard:digest day=2026-03-04 -->\", \"**Jobs run:** 0\", \"**Failures:** 0\", \"**Spend:** $0.00\"} {\n+\t\tif !strings.Contains(zero, want) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"zero digest lacks %q:\\n%s\", want, zero)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\td := Data{\n+\t\tDay:   \"2026-03-04\",\n+\t\tQueue: map[string]int{\"ard:x @evil\": 1},\n+\t\tJobs:  map[state.RoleKey]state.JobCounts{{Stage: \"worker\", Role: \"Bad Role@x\"}: {Done: 1, Failed: 2}},\n+\t\tTotal: state.Spend{USD: 1.5, Unpriced: 2},\n+\t}\n+\tout := Render(d)\n+\tif strings.Contains(out, \"@\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"worker/? | 2\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"2 steps reported no cost\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"**Jobs run:** 3\") {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"render:\\n%s\", out)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestIntervalAndClaims(t *testing.T) {\n+\tl := NewLoop(Deps{})\n+\tif l.Claims() || l.Name() != \"digest\" || l.Interval(nil) != 10*time.Minute {\n+\t\tt.Error(\"loop identity\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func controllerEnv() controller.Env { return controller.Env{} }\ndiff --git a/internal/digest/render.go b/internal/digest/render.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..130b5d9\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/digest/render.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@\n+package digest\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"regexp\"\n+\t\"sort\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state\"\n+)\n+\n+// Data is what one digest reports. Day is the UTC day covered (2006-01-02).\n+type Data struct {\n+\tDay   string\n+\tQueue map[string]int\n+\tJobs  map[state.RoleKey]state.JobCounts\n+\tSpend map[state.RoleKey]state.Spend\n+\tTotal state.Spend\n+}\n+\n+func (d Data) counts() (jobs, failed int) {\n+\tfor _, c := range d.Jobs {\n+\t\tjobs += c.Done + c.Failed\n+\t\tfailed += c.Failed\n+\t}\n+\treturn\n+}\n+\n+var safeName = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z0-9._/:-]+$`)\n+\n+func safe(s string) string {\n+\tif safeName.MatchString(s) {\n+\t\treturn s\n+\t}\n+\treturn \"?\"\n+}\n+\n+// Render is the digest comment. It holds only numbers, the day and label and\n+// role names; no agent text, no issue titles and no \"@\".\n+func Render(d Data) string {\n+\tvar b strings.Builder\n+\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"<!-- ard:digest day=%s -->\\n\", safe(d.Day))\n+\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"**ard · daily digest for %s (UTC)**\\n\\n\", safe(d.Day))\n+\n+\tb.WriteString(\"**Queue depth** (open issues by label)\\n\\n\")\n+\tif len(d.Queue) == 0 {\n+\t\tb.WriteString(\"No open issue carries an `ard:` label.\\n\")\n+\t} else {\n+\t\tb.WriteString(\"| Label | Issues |\\n|---|---|\\n\")\n+\t\tnames := make([]string, 0, len(d.Queue))\n+\t\tfor n := range d.Queue {\n+\t\t\tnames = append(names, n)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tsort.Strings(names)\n+\t\tfor _, n := range names {\n+\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"| `%s` | %d |\\n\", safe(n), d.Queue[n])\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\n+\tjobs, failed := d.counts()\n+\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"\\n**Jobs run:** %d\\n\\n**Failures:** %d\\n\", jobs, failed)\n+\tkeys := make([]state.RoleKey, 0, len(d.Jobs))\n+\tfor k, c := range d.Jobs {\n+\t\tif c.Failed > 0 {\n+\t\t\tkeys = append(keys, k)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tsort.Slice(keys, func(i, j int) bool {\n+\t\tif keys[i].Stage != keys[j].Stage {\n+\t\t\treturn keys[i].Stage < keys[j].Stage\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn keys[i].Role < keys[j].Role\n+\t})\n+\tif len(keys) > 0 {\n+\t\tb.WriteString(\"\\n| Role | Failed |\\n|---|---|\\n\")\n+\t\tfor _, k := range keys {\n+\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"| %s/%s | %d |\\n\", safe(k.Stage), safe(k.Role), d.Jobs[k].Failed)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\n+\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \"\\n**Spend:** $%.2f\", d.Total.USD)\n+\tif d.Total.Unpriced > 0 {\n+\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&b, \" (%d steps reported no cost and count as $0)\", d.Total.Unpriced)\n+\t}\n+\tb.WriteString(\"\\n\\nOn a subscription the dollar figure is an estimate.\\n\")\n+\treturn b.String()\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/servecmd/digest.go b/internal/servecmd/digest.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..26bfb1d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/servecmd/digest.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@\n+package servecmd\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/controller\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/digest\"\n+)\n+\n+// digestLoop posts the daily status-issue digest: queue depth by label, jobs\n+// run, failures and spend for the previous UTC day.\n+func digestLoop(w *wiring) controller.Loop {\n+\treturn digest.NewLoop(digest.Deps{\n+\t\tStore: w.Store, Reader: w.Reader, Effects: w.Effects,\n+\t\tStatusIssue: func() int { return int(w.statusIssue.Load()) },\n+\t\tLog:         w.Log, Now: w.budgetNow,\n+\t})\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/servecmd/loops_test.go b/internal/servecmd/loops_test.go\nindex 52a8c52..51ae856 100644\n--- a/internal/servecmd/loops_test.go\n+++ b/internal/servecmd/loops_test.go\n@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ func TestServeUnknownLoopFailsFirst(t *testing.T) {\n \n // The loop names registerLoops' constructors report are the known names.\n func TestKnownLoopsMatchLoopNames(t *testing.T) {\n-\twant := []string{\"scanners\", \"stale\", \"triage\", \"workers\", \"reviewers\", \"reviewfix\", \"merger\", \"prwatch\", \"janitor\", \"reaper\", \"budget\"}\n+\twant := []string{\"scanners\", \"stale\", \"triage\", \"workers\", \"reviewers\", \"reviewfix\", \"merger\", \"prwatch\", \"janitor\", \"reaper\", \"budget\", \"digest\"}\n \tif !reflect.DeepEqual(knownLoops, want) {\n \t\tt.Errorf(\"knownLoops = %v, want %v\", knownLoops, want)\n \t}\ndiff --git a/internal/servecmd/rebuild_test.go b/internal/servecmd/rebuild_test.go\nindex eba32d8..e88783f 100644\n--- a/internal/servecmd/rebuild_test.go\n+++ b/internal/servecmd/rebuild_test.go\n@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ func TestDefaultLoopsIncludeTheScannersLoop(t *testing.T) {\n \t}\n \tdefer w.Scanners.Close()\n \tloops := registerLoops(w)\n-\tif len(loops) != 12 || loops[0].Name() != \"scanners\" || loops[1].Name() != \"stale\" || loops[2].Name() != \"triage\" || loops[3].Name() != \"workers\" || loops[4].Name() != \"reviewers\" || loops[5].Name() != \"reviewfix\" || loops[6].Name() != \"merger\" || loops[7].Name() != \"prwatch\" || loops[8].Name() != \"janitor\" || loops[9].Name() != \"reaper\" || loops[10].Name() != \"costs\" || loops[11].Name() != \"budget\" ||\n+\tif len(loops) != 13 || loops[0].Name() != \"scanners\" || loops[1].Name() != \"stale\" || loops[2].Name() != \"triage\" || loops[3].Name() != \"workers\" || loops[4].Name() != \"reviewers\" || loops[5].Name() != \"reviewfix\" || loops[6].Name() != \"merger\" || loops[7].Name() != \"prwatch\" || loops[8].Name() != \"janitor\" || loops[9].Name() != \"reaper\" || loops[10].Name() != \"costs\" || loops[11].Name() != \"budget\" || loops[12].Name() != \"digest\" ||\n \t\t!loops[0].Claims() || !loops[1].Claims() || !loops[2].Claims() || !loops[3].Claims() || !loops[4].Claims() || !loops[5].Claims()